==German==

===Alternative forms===
* [[scheissen]] {{qualifier|Switzerland}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|schizen|schīzen|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|skītanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|skeyd|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|sḱeyd-||to part with, separate, cut off|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Middle Low German {{term|schiten|schīten|lang=gml}}, Dutch {{term|schijten|lang=nl}}, and English (verb) ''[[shit]]'', Danish {{term|skide|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaɪ̯sn̩/|/ˈʃaɪ̯sən/|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|scheißt|schiss|geschissen}}

# {{vulgar|lang=de}} to [[shit]]
#: ''Ich '''scheiß'''' mir gleich in die Hose!''

====Conjugation====
Before 1996, the past tense form was {{term|schiß}}, but, per the 1996 German Spelling Reform, the correct spelling is now {{term|schiss}}.
{{de-conj-strong|scheiß|schiss|geschissen|h||||a|a|||a}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|vulgar|to shit}} [[kacken]], [[koten]], [[Stuhlgang haben]]

